+**Q1: Synchronization Strategy (Shared State)**
+- **Approved Answer:**
+  - Protect shared state variables in handlers using `std::mutex` with `std::lock_guard` (Option B) for general complex state
+  - Use `std::atomic<T>` for scalar/flag states (Option A)
+
+**Q2: Handler Invocation Lock Scope**
+- **Approved Answer:**
+  - Option A (Release lock before handler invocation)
+  - ServiceRegistry lock is released before invoking the handler to avoid deadlocks during recursive calls or nested registrations
+
+**Q3: Null Endpoint & Silent Drop Mitigation**
+- **Approved Answer:**
+  - Add explicit warning logging in send_error() if endpoint_ is null or if endpoint_->send_to() returns false
+  - Ensure MessageRouter logs error details when a method is unregistered
+
+**Q4: Error Message Type & Return Code**
+- **Approved Answer:**
+  - Message Type for unregistered method response is ERR (0x81) per SOME/IP spec
+  - Note: RQ-08-001 "0x02" reference was a typo mapping to NOTIFICATION
+  - Return code is 0x01 (E_NOT_OK) or 0xFF (E_UNKNOWN)
+  - Echo Client ID and Session ID headers
